meta {
  name: Split PDF
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/forms/pdfengines/split
  body: multipart
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/pdf
}

body:multipart {
  files[]: @file(./files/sample.pdf)
  splitMode: intervals
  splitSpan: 1
  splitUnify: false
}

docs {
  ## Split PDF

  Splits a PDF file into multiple PDFs using the Gotenberg PDF engines API.

  ### Form Fields

  | Field        | Type    | Description                                                                 |
  |--------------|---------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | files[]      | File    | The PDF file(s) to split.                                                   |
  | splitMode    | String  | The split mode: `intervals`, `pages`, or `r-intervals`.                     |
  | splitSpan    | Integer | The span to use for splitting (e.g., every N pages).                        |
  | splitUnify   | Boolean | Whether to unify the split results into a single PDF. Default: `false`.     |

  ### Split Modes

  - **intervals**: Split every N pages (defined by `splitSpan`).
  - **pages**: Split at specific page numbers (comma-separated in `splitSpan`).
  - **r-intervals**: Split in reverse intervals.

  ### Response

  Returns the split PDF file(s). If multiple files are produced and `splitUnify` is `false`,
  the response will be a ZIP archive containing each split PDF.

  ### Example

  To split a PDF every 2 pages:
  ```
  splitMode: intervals
  splitSpan: 2
  ```

  To split at specific pages (e.g., pages 2 and 4):
  ```
  splitMode: pages
  splitSpan: 2,4
  ```
}
